zl1 -- the SECOND heat cause (cpufreq governor), the ALTERNATING design, FOUR device runs with the
WINDOW-MEAN reading, 2026-09-26
====================================================================================================

ONE BOOT THROUGHOUT: boot_id 2fbf9f8e-deea-4955-ad0c-6bddf0fb14f5 -- re-read before the series and
after the last run: UNCHANGED, and it is the SAME boot the six snapshot runs of docs 176 used (the
series started at /proc/uptime 32056 and ended at 33657, 1601 s = about 27 minutes for four runs of
4 pairs). Four cores read `interactive` after every run (each run restores it in its own EXIT trap
and re-reads it), and they read `interactive` at the end of the series. Nothing was flashed, no
partition was written, no block device was opened, no service was restarted, the container was never
stopped.

WHAT THE FOUR RUNS ARE. The alternating design (docs 175) -- 4 pairs of (fix window, pinned window),
order alternating inside each pair, 30 s windows, 5 s settle -- on the real phone, four times back to
back, with the two docs-177 fixes in place in the thermal instrument.

WHY THIS RUN EXISTS. The same design ran six times on this phone on this boot with the OLD reading
(docs 176) and printed +2.03, -0.58, +2.48, +5.88, +2.27, +2.30 C -- four different numbers and one
of them negative -- because the instrument's zone table was a single sample of the window's LAST
INSTANT and a tsens zone moves 3-4 C inside a 48 s window. docs 176's closing line named the fix and
this stage is it: the window's temperature is now the MEAN of samples walked once a second across it.

THE HEADLINE -- FOUR RUNS, AND THEY SAY THE SAME THING.

