   4    thermal_zone9  (tsens_tz_sensor8)   +2.10 C   0.18   [1.74, 2.46]      cost-measured

  range of the four readings: 2.10 .. 2.73 C; all four intervals are above the 0.2 C this experiment
  resolves, and none of them contains it.

  THE SAME DESIGN, THE SAME PHONE, THE SAME BOOT, WITH THE OLD READING (docs 176):
    +2.03 (se 0.38)   -0.58   +2.48   +5.88 (se 0.97)   +2.27   +2.30 C
  -- four different numbers, a sign flip, and four different primary zones. The difference between
  the two sets is the READING, and that was measured during that series: on its run 6 a 2 s by-name
  sampler running BESIDE the instrument read the window MEANS on the same windows and got +0.61
  where the snapshot got +2.30 on thermal_zone18.

  What the mean did NOT change: the sign. Every reading in either set that was a reading (rather than
  an artifact) is positive. What it changed is the ERROR BAR: 0.10-0.18 now against 0.38-0.97 then.

SECTION 1 -- INSTRUMENT IDENTITY, AND WHAT THE FOUR RUNS ACTUALLY EXECUTED
====================================================================================================

  governor instrument  /tmp/zl1-governor-temp-ab.sh  md5 a148b614c35e59c640676c5f27c7b368
  thermal instrument   /tmp/zl1-thermal.sh           md5 f42f0785ee0eb4033e51227d9ef684bf
  launcher             /tmp/gov-mean-quad.sh         (copied back verbatim, section 6)

The governor instrument is byte-identical to scripts/device/zl1-governor-temp-ab.sh as committed
before this stage. The repository copy has since gained three comment lines and one `say` string
carrying the re-measured wall-clock figures (13.8 s / 23.8 s). That the difference is text and not
code was checked with `diff` between the deployed copy and the repository copy: three hunks, each of
them a comment sentence continued or one `say` string split across two lines. No code line differs,
so the four runs below used the instrument as committed.

The thermal instrument is the NEW one: `zone_mean`/`zone_spread`, the once-a-second sample loop with
the sample's cost subtracted from its own sleep, and `wsecs` (each window's own measured seconds) as
the divisor of every rate. Its first window on this phone, before the series:

