====================================================================================================
SECTION 2 -- THE THREE COSTS, MEASURED ON THIS PHONE (why the second fix was needed at all)
====================================================================================================

Read on the same boot, with /proc/uptime as the clock (the RTC reads 1970):

  one walk of the 38 thermal zones (76 forks)                  0.30 s
  one walk of /proc for all 621 processes                      4.58 s
  `zl1-thermal.sh --seconds 10`, end to end                    23.8 s   (28.1 s before the fix)
  the interval between its two /proc/stat reads                20.7 s   (printed by the fixed instrument)

So the numerator of every rate was a 20.7 s window while the denominator was 10 s. The zone walk and
BOTH process walks are inside the window -- which is why the two numbers differ by a factor of two
rather than by a few percent.

====================================================================================================
SECTION 3 -- THE FOUR VERDICTS, VERBATIM, IN FULL
====================================================================================================

Each run's own log follows, untouched. The per-pair tables, the control (the phone's own drift,
measured between the fix windows), the balance line, the pre-registration and the verdict are all in
them; the four logs have the same shape because they are the same design.

