                  back -- writable in fact, and every core agrees on what it read.

== the alternating design -- 4 pair(s) of (fix 'interactive', pinned 'performance')
   Every pair is two proved writes and two windows of 30s, with 5s after each write. The
   reading is the difference 'performance' minus 'interactive' WITHIN a pair, so whatever the phone does
   over the ~6 minutes of this run it does to both halves of a pair and cancels in the difference.
   NO pre-hold and NO wait: neither window has to be a STATE, because the comparison is between two
   windows 30s apart rather than between readings taken 8 windows apart.
   The risk is held the other way round from the three-window design: pinning is written, settled and
   held for exactly ONE window, then the fix is written back -- so the phone is never more than one
   window away from the state this script found it in.
   pair 1/4: fix window first, then the other one
